      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing a Provider**\n\nI've decided to proceed with Google Cloud Text-to-Speech. It's a solid choice given its widespread adoption and generally strong performance. Next up is implementing the voice listing and selection functions within the `select_voice.py` script, which will need to connect with the Google Cloud API.\n\n\n**Defining the API Interaction**\n\nI'm now prioritizing the API interaction within `select_voice.py`, focusing on how to list available voices. My focus is on making the provider, Google Cloud Text-to-Speech, identifiable. I'll need to figure out the specific client initialization required, and then define a function to list those voices for any given locale. This listing function will demonstrate how to successfully use the Google Cloud Text-to-Speech API.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789861884248,
          "start": 1789861881747
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc14e793001wnwbEqq6cJQHiM",
